{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/830405-soo","id":830405,"title":"Soo....?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-15T12:26:02-08:00","id":830405,"title":"Soo....?","content":"<a href=\"http://imagonem.org/2016/02/15/white-wolfs-lead-storyteller-there-will-be-a-release-in-2016/\" target=\"_blank\">http://imagonem.org/2016/02/15/white...lease-in-2016/</a><br /> Here's an interview with the lead storyteller and I may be reading into it a bit much but it seems like a lot of our fears about the new Werewolf may be true.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:liberation-sans-1\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Will the Werewolves remain crypto fascist eco-terrorist?</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:liberation-sans-1, liberation-sans-2, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">More than they have ever been. Global Warming has released the Wyrm-tide. The end of the Impergium (ancient Werewolves hunting humans to keep their numbers manageable) seems like a terrible mistake in retrospect.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>Also seems like they'll be reinserting more ham-fisted politics into the game for the sake of edginess and bad taste. In my opinion the WoD was at its worst when it got involved in this kind of thing and over simplified and cheapened complex political and social issues. Now I'm a pretty left-leaning person but Werewolf is already preachy enough as it is and it sounds like they'll be making it even worse.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:liberation-sans-1, liberation-sans-2, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">inability to deal with and integrate real-world events in the setting. If you can write about the Holocaust, you can write about 9/11. Fear is the death of creativity. The game was always best in the hands of storytellers who dared to place the story close to reality, often in their own cities, featuring real places and people.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:liberation-sans-1, liberation-sans-2, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">I just want someone to pat me on the back and tell me that it will all be ok. (Forgive the formatting issues.)</span></span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3198-lunar-falcon","name":"Lunar Falcon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3198_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T13:02:49-08:00","id":830436,"title":"","content":"So let me get this straight....Onyx Path will continue to put out a nostalgia line so people like me who are not interested in what BNS is putting out can still get our fix for new books while Paradox will be putting out the other stuff? If that's the case I guess I can just fight the power and vote with my money to support the line I enjoy the most. If there are enough people like me, money will talk. (Again this is assuming Paradox will be putting out stuff like the BNS stuff where we have male Furies and what not)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T15:18:46-08:00","id":830544,"title":"","content":"That reads like one of the worst things written in the 90s, and goes out of its way to slam the CofD for no reason. I'm also getting the impression that they don't like Exalted very much..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:liberation-sans-1\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Onyx Path also have a license to produce nostalgia books for the classic WoD settings. These are official but set in the same nebulous \u201deternal nineties\u201d, using the old-school buckets-of-dice-system featured in the original lines. </span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure that the 20th Anniversary Editions have all painted a very modern picture, not one of the early 90s. They have smartphones, they have cars that can drive themselves... honestly, this outlook may be more troubling than the terrible, loaded question about Werewolf that thoroughly ignores any mythological context to the existence of Garou or Fera. I'm not really sure who this interview is made to appeal to, honestly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T15:52:32-08:00","id":830571,"title":"","content":"What really gets me is the whole &quot;rethink the Impegrium&quot; part. Sure, some times disagree, but vast majority saw it as a mistake for other reasons than letting humans spread. The text sounds like they want to return to the narrow streotypes and rarr style that the 1st ed had. Not the much deeper revised that questioned the methods and the 20th eds which even offered some positivity to the setting.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T17:01:57-08:00","id":830612,"title":"","content":"I dont see &quot;rethink the impegrium&quot;, I see &quot;..seems like a terrible mistake in retrospect.&quot; I keep looking, maybe I'm missing it.<br /> <br /> I dont think much was said enough to do anything with other than jump to conclusions. But that seems like fun. Here's hoping OP keeps to get making the Nostalgia pieces I like so much and they leave cWoD alone and maybe make a few video games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T21:12:12-08:00","id":830788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Somuchlove</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/830405-soo?p=830612#post830612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dont see &quot;rethink the impegrium&quot;, I see &quot;..seems like a terrible mistake in retrospect.&quot; I keep looking, maybe I'm missing it.<br /> <br /> I dont think much was said enough to do anything with other than jump to conclusions. But that seems like fun. Here's hoping OP keeps to get making the Nostalgia pieces I like so much and they leave cWoD alone and maybe make a few video games.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, he could have taken a few more sentences to deconstruct the loaded question and reframe the game's underpinnings, but he didn't. A fanciful comparison to an old lick rising from torpor got more consideration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T01:06:16-08:00","id":830889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lunar Falcon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/830405-soo#post830405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:liberation-sans-1, liberation-sans-2, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">I just want someone to pat me on the back and tell me that it will all be ok. (Forgive the formatting issues.)</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>There, there... everything will be ok. They can never take W20 or any of the old stuff from you.<br /> <br /> I've read the interview first thing this morning. I cannot say I'm thrilled. It shows a fundamental cluelessness about Werewolf's tone and themes. It's also kind of like they were into Vampire back in early 90s and never seem to have seen what was done with the WoD over the following 20 years. A lot of the imagery and mindset presented seems set in a different time. Which is odd, as I'd have expected us to be the ones who are more fixated on the old rather then the new. Also it's condescending and rude to CoD, which I don't appreciate, even though I'm not it's biggest fan.<br /> <br /> We'll get W20 support for a while more, but I'm not sure they will want to dillute the singular One World of Darkness with a &quot;Classic&quot; or &quot;Alternate Reality&quot; imprint once they have the new thing up and running.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T03:02:33-08:00","id":830927,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I guess that that Onyx Path will at some point stop with W20 Setting books. For, it doesn't make sense to rebrand the nWoD and then split the cWoD into one that has metaplot advanced in a way that really changed the setting, and another nostalgia line that just hast time advance but with minimal repercussions for the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T03:15:38-08:00","id":830936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/830405-soo?p=830788#post830788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, he could have taken a few more sentences to deconstruct the loaded question and reframe the game's underpinnings, but he didn't. A fanciful comparison to an old lick rising from torpor got more consideration.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could have done, but chose not too. With many possible reasons as to why. None that we'll know for fact unless answered later, what we do know is that this was a brief q&amp;a. Hardly enough time for detailed insight to the movements and machinations of what is to come and to be.<br /> <br /> We also hear in the first answer that all plans will be secret until they are not. Until then anything we dread or dare to conclude will simply be a conjuring of our own fearful or hopeful conjurations.<br /> <br /> I await with patient intrigue and curious interest until the curtains are pulled back to reveal what hides behind. Because what other choice is there? Very vampire of him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T09:19:07-08:00","id":831073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/830405-soo?p=830889#post830889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There, there... everything will be ok. They can never take W20 or any of the old stuff from you.<br /> <br /> I've read the interview first thing this morning. I cannot say I'm thrilled. It shows a fundamental cluelessness about Werewolf's tone and themes. It's also kind of like they were into Vampire back in early 90s and never seem to have seen what was done with the WoD over the following 20 years. A lot of the imagery and mindset presented seems set in a different time. Which is odd, as I'd have expected us to be the ones who are more fixated on the old rather then the new. Also it's condescending and rude to CoD, which I don't appreciate, even though I'm not it's biggest fan.<br /> <br /> We'll get W20 support for a while more, but I'm not sure they will want to dillute the singular One World of Darkness with a &quot;Classic&quot; or &quot;Alternate Reality&quot; imprint once they have the new thing up and running.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>There were several disrespectful and backhanded compliments in that interview.<br /> <br /> It sounds like they are tossing aside some of the important lessons WW learned over the course of the original run. In games set in a pure fantasy world it's easy to portray politics and religion without being too overbearing or offensive because no one has a real stake in those concepts. If they go overboard with real world issues they risk alienating a lot of their potential audience and pissing a lot of people off which isn't a smart move for a company trying to reach new people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":3198,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3198-lunar-falcon","user":"Lunar Falcon","date":".  Autocorrect sucks. 02-16-2016, 12:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3198-lunar-falcon","name":"Lunar Falcon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3198_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T12:06:23-08:00","id":831199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lunar Falcon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/830405-soo?p=831073#post831073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There were several disrespectful and backhanded compliments in that interview.<br /> <br /> It sounds like they are tossing aside some of the important lessons WW learned over the course of the original run. In games set in a pure fantasy world it's easy to portray politics and religion without being too overbearing or offensive because no one has a real stake in those concepts. If they go overboard with real world issues they risk alienating a lot of their potential audience and pissing a lot of people off which isn't a smart move for a company trying to reach new people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Meh. Let them be pissed. People get bent out of shape over everything and anything nowadays. Personally, if I have to choose between books that might make some people angry, and those that are so sanitized and banal that they never could possibly offend anyone, I would choose the former.<br /> <br /> Books don't offend me. If a published work has stuff in it that is wrongheaded, I just figure the writer is a moron and move on. No pain on my end.<br /> <br /> I am more worried that every current and historical figure turns out to be a space alien spy...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T16:16:18-08:00","id":831346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/830405-soo?p=831199#post831199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Meh. Let them be pissed. People get bent out of shape over everything and anything nowadays. Personally, if I have to choose between books that might make some people angry, and those that are so sanitized and banal that they never could possibly offend anyone, I would choose the former.<br /> <br /> Books don't offend me. If a published work has stuff in it that is wrongheaded, I just figure the writer is a moron and move on. No pain on my end.<br /> <br /> I am more worried that every current and historical figure turns out to be a space alien spy...</div> </div> </div> </div>To rouse rather than just pointlessly shock, hopefully.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T16:54:23-08:00","id":831366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/830405-soo?p=831199#post831199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Meh. Let them be pissed. People get bent out of shape over everything and anything nowadays. Personally, if I have to choose between books that might make some people angry, and those that are so sanitized and banal that they never could possibly offend anyone, I would choose the former.<br /> <br /> Books don't offend me. If a published work has stuff in it that is wrongheaded, I just figure the writer is a moron and move on. No pain on my end.<br /> <br /> I am more worried that every current and historical figure turns out to be a space alien spy...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> But if you find the writer to be a moron do you continue to buy products from that writer? I think Lunar Falcon's main point was that if its done poorly its going to cost Paradox fans, both old and new.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T17:45:10-08:00","id":831383,"title":"","content":"I really get the feeling that since this guy was working on the ccp wod mmo, he saw that it was going no where and just decided to pick up the IP on a lark since his own company was making bank. <br /> <br /> So really he is just living the dream of setting the plot to whatever he thinks is cool, Gothic punk is dead and has been replaced with hot topic edge lord.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T22:33:08-08:00","id":831512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/830405-soo?p=831383#post831383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So really he is just living the dream of setting the plot to whatever he thinks is cool, Gothic punk is dead and has been replaced with hot topic edge lord.</div> </div> </div> </div>At least we won't have South Park's PC Principal in charge, that's for sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>One thing is for sure: nothing is for sure.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/83-evolved_lupus","name":"evolved_lupus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.c