},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T19:36:48-08:00","id":832269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/830405-soo?p=832125#post832125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think some people, like myself, might still be reeling from all of the wait whats that the BNS Werewolf contained, apparently given a stamp of approval by WWP.</div> </div> </div> </div>BNS? I am curious now. Details if you don't mind? And I hope people understand. I do sympathize with the trepidation and coarse words can certainly make that worse. But mostly I am in wait and see mode as it were because I've yet to see anything really concrete to actually make a critique of and not to sound an old bastard but it's too tiring for me to take what we have and speculate on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T19:52:05-08:00","id":832280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/830405-soo?p=832269#post832269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> BNS? I am curious now. Details if you don't mind? And I hope people understand. I do sympathize with the trepidation and coarse words can certainly make that worse. But mostly I am in wait and see mode as it were because I've yet to see anything really concrete to actually make a critique of and not to sound an old bastard but it's too tiring for me to take what we have and speculate on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I posted a number of issues I had <a href=\"http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?764192-MET-Werewolf-The-Apocalypse-Beta-Playtest&amp;p=19342291#post19342291\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>. There are also issues with the virtual gutting of the Umbra that are far more of an impact on Werewolf than the Avatar Storm was for Mage, since in Werewolf anything that has its spirit destroyed breaks down and ceases to exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T01:40:41-08:00","id":832390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/830405-soo?p=832280#post832280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I posted a number of issues I had <a href=\"http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?764192-MET-Werewolf-The-Apocalypse-Beta-Playtest&amp;p=19342291#post19342291\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>. There are also issues with the virtual gutting of the Umbra that are far more of an impact on Werewolf than the Avatar Storm was for Mage, since in Werewolf anything that has its spirit destroyed breaks down and ceases to exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>From that discussion there, I'd say a few things. First of all, the whole jobs thing. While I can understand the point, the fact is that that aspect has all ready been mastered in Forsaken. In general as well, Forsaken is far more on-the-street type of werewolf, with issues relating to local conflicts over global ones.<br /> <br /> Apocalypse, meanwhile, always struck me as a more fantasy type game. The garou are great heroes, and as such they aren't as involved in everyday life (that, and kinfolk are there to do it). Their mistakes and culture are far more separate, because they have a much clearer one to the uratha.<br /> <br /> And this is also why the reason for this thread bothers me. WtA is at its best when its questioning and doubting what the garou believe in and do. As well, in Rage Across the World 20th there is some really good talk of conservation in a smart way. Going back to the nineties way, where the discussion wasn't there as much, would be bad.<br /> <br /> (Of course, we might be over reacting and the new edition would not turn out that bad. But discussion is still good.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T02:05:04-08:00","id":832397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/830405-soo?p=832280#post832280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I posted a number of issues I had <a href=\"http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?764192-MET-Werewolf-The-Apocalypse-Beta-Playtest&amp;p=19342291#post19342291\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>. There are also issues with the virtual gutting of the Umbra that are far more of an impact on Werewolf than the Avatar Storm was for Mage, since in Werewolf anything that has its spirit destroyed breaks down and ceases to exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Had to remember what BNS was then finally clicked it was By Night Studios. Never followed their end of things when Onyx Path started and they took over the MET stuff. Stopped LARPing a little before my daughter was born in the early 2000's and had no idea they were changing stuff like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T02:16:27-08:00","id":832401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/830405-soo?p=832269#post832269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> BNS? I am curious now. Details if you don't mind? And I hope people understand. I do sympathize with the trepidation and coarse words can certainly make that worse. But mostly I am in wait and see mode as it were because I've yet to see anything really concrete to actually make a critique of and not to sound an old bastard but it's too tiring for me to take what we have and speculate on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>We also had a discussion <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/804780-bns-kickstarter-for-met-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=806995#post806995\">here on the Werewolf forum. </a><br /> You might find a lot more stuff from the Gamma slice in there that's being discussed in addition to Dino's concerns. It's... not very in line with anything we've seen in Werewolf before. The reason why both he and I were being worried is this bit on their kickstarter page:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BNS Kickstarter</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><ul><li>An <b>updated story</b> that frames the epic tale of the Garou for the 21st century. We are honored to be working closely with <b>White Wolf\u2019s Lead Storyteller Martin Elricsson</b> to infuse <i>MET: Werewolf</i> with a <b>powerful narrative and mature story</b> that helps usher in the new era of the <i>World of Darkness</i>.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>The further Interviews and commentary implied that this is the start of the One World of Darkness. So at worst, this is what it will look like, at best it's what Martin sees as reasonable. That does not sound good to my Werewolf loving ears.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T03:01:19-08:00","id":832414,"title":"","content":"I'm not too worried. What ever happens i'll still have enough material and my own imagination to keep playing with others for decades. If the setting becomes something I dont care for I just wont collect the books and keep playing classic Classic style. Just like I did between Apocalypse and W20.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T07:21:24-08:00","id":834415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Somuchlove</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/830405-soo?p=832414#post832414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not too worried. What ever happens i'll still have enough material and my own imagination to keep playing with others for decades. If the setting becomes something I dont care for I just wont collect the books and keep playing classic Classic style. Just like I did between Apocalypse and W20.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly this, I will probably buy the new book cannibalize anything I like and update as I want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T23:19:57-08:00","id":836267,"title":"","content":"&quot;Anything that smells of Fantasy. The attempt to create a deep mythology by linking the setting to Exalted was the worst choice ever. That was the last step in WoD\u2019d death-march from being an artistic horror-IP to full on immature, escapist Urban Fantasy.&quot;<br /> <br /> I wasn't a huge fan of Exalted, but that was one of my favorite things about it; that it could be an alternate, ancient pre-history for the World of Darkness. I was actually a little sad to hear they had moved away from that. Tying the WOD to Exalted had very little effect on the WOD itself, as far as I could tell. And ANYTHING that &quot;smells of fantasy?&quot; That's dangerously close to dumping on Mage, Changeling, and even the Dark Ages line. I'm not sure I want to hear a critique of escapism from a guy who clearly thinks he's actually a vampire.<br /> <br /> &quot;The inability to deal with and integrate real-world events in the setting. If you can write about the Holocaust, you can write about 9/11.&quot; They did.<br /> <br /> I'm glad they're focusing on the old World of Darkness, as it's my favorite offering from White Wolf, but that interview doesn't give me a lot of confidence in their motives or plans.<br /> <br /> As far as the Garou remaining &quot;crypto-fascist eco terrorists&quot; (pretentious much dot jpg), environmental concern has come roaring back lately, so I'm not too worried about that being addressed.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7445-viking-funeral","name":"Viking Funeral","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7445_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T23:46:41-08:00","id":836273,"title":"","content":"I think the idea to market Exalted as an pre-historic WoD was mostly a design choice within Exalted and never had any effect on the WoD, especially since it was given up, before Exalted was finished, iirc. So all that remains are some ads with that idea in the back of some books....<br /> <br /> For me the downfall of Vampire came with the broad availability of Paths of Enlightenment. They just felt like a means to bypass the loss of humanity, that I always saw as the core element of the game.<br /> <br /> As for werewolf - I didn't see the garou as &quot;eco terrorists&quot; ever, because they themselves don't see their actions that way. Sure, humans might perceive their actions that way, out of a need to fill in the blanks and make sense of otherwise unexplainable acts. But garou themselves don't set out to strike the fear of ecological destruction into the heart of mankind. They set out to be proud warriors to find, track and kill the minions of the Wyrm - you know - wherever they dwell and breed. Forcing changes upon them by altering the world, changing the lost cub to actually &quot;raised as true born garou&quot; - warriors, making gifts somehow work different, destroy all cearns and make the garou less dependant on a specific location all seem choices that might have been great if Mark Rhein-Hagen had had them 25 years ago. Now the glimpses I've seem from it almost seem like a different game altogether.<br /> <br /> I feel the constant need to change the setting has ruined Marvel and DC and the Dark Eye RPG (which is huge here in Germany). I don't buy their products anymore, I get synopsis of their changing universes at youtube or fan wikis. Leaning this way with the WoD I find is a move that might not sit well with older fans, but might attract young ones. In any case, it seems to remove the focus of the games from character driven personal adult plots to meta-plot world changing ride-alongs.<br /> <br /> I mean, I don't know how you guys game, but for me it is two game nights a month, divided up amongst all the games. And bi-monthly werewolf LARP weekends. In any case, I wouldn't have time in any game to deal with the plot the ST invented, yet alone deal with changes White Wolf forces into the game world. Just saying, since 10 years seems to be the interval for all the comic book universe changes...<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-24T02:06:08-08:00","id":836305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/830405-soo?p=836273#post836273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the idea to market Exalted as an pre-historic WoD was mostly a design choice within Exalted and never had any effect on the WoD, especially since it was given up, before Exalted was finished, iirc. So all that remains are some ads with that idea in the back of some books....</div> </div> </div> </div>It was abandoned in both lines. There are some references, like the names of some of the antagonist and a lot of similar ideas in the Underworld, but they're totally different beasts. You'd have to have a very skewed perception of Exalted to see much of WoD in it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/830405-soo?p=836273#post836273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, I don't know how you guys game, but for me it is two game nights a month, divided up amongst all the games. And bi-monthly werewolf LARP weekends. In any case, I wouldn't have time in any game to deal with the plot the ST invented, yet alone deal with changes White Wolf forces into the game world. Just saying, since 10 years seems to be the interval for all the comic book universe changes...</div> </div> </div> </div>It's... worse than that these days. 4-5 years is the maximum you can get without a big reboot. Even shorter occasionaly.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":1182,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","user":"Asmodai","date":". 02-24-2016, 05:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-24T04:44:50-08:00","id":836342,"title":"","content":"Problem is, these world changing mega events aren't really the best stories nor is &quot;the whole multiverse/universe is at stake&quot; a huge selling point anymore. The best critically acclaimed series as far as I know are stand alone stories, sometimes even non-canon stories.<br /> <br /> And compared to the Dark Eye or the &quot;Living Greyhawk/Forgotten Realms/Kalamar/what ever&quot; games I think the WoD had the benefit, that it was a Setting that evolved with the real woberld it was based, without much need of world altering scenarios and stuff like that...<br /> Sure, there was metaplot and Gangrels leaving Camarilla, and Stargazer leaving Garou Nation, and Ravnos being killed and so on.... but a lot of people I know ignored them (for they were not that fundamental, that one couldn't just play around them, if one had a game already running and just wanted to update to the newest rule set.<br /> <br /> With W20 that changed, for it became more restricting with stepping sideways and finding pre-change cubs that made adapting harder, imo, What I read of BNS's Age of Apocalypse Werewolf seems even more describing a Setting where even the rules force you to use the given Setting, instead of being applicable to a werewolf game in all eras (including how Apocalpyse was before BNS's changes to the Setting). If that is true for the IV Edition of Werewolf, too. The books really seem a lot less practical for all these people, who would like to play on the way apocalypse is now (but with better mechanics).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}